{
  "id": "runner_01_clicks",
  "side": "Runner",
  "title": "Clicks and credits",
  "intro": "You are the Runner. Each turn you get 4 clicks (one more than the Corp) and, unlike the Corp, no forced draw. Your hand is your grip, your deck is your stack, your discard pile is your heap. Credits pay for everything, so making money is the first skill.\n\nThis lesson: keep your hand, play Sure Gamble, and take a couple of basic actions.",
  "outro": "Sure Gamble turned 5 credits into 9 for one click — four credits better than clicking four times. Events are one-shot cards: play them, resolve them, they go to the heap. Next: installing a program so you can get through ice.",
  "corp_deck": "the_syndicate_starter",
  "runner_deck": "the_catalyst_starter",
